  "body": "## What changed\n\nSaved cut recipes hold an operation's parameters, its tool name, and its workpiece material. A user library stores them in `recipes.camrecipes`, with a `camcraft-recipes/1` envelope. The folder is `CAMCRAFT_RECIPES`, else `<platform data dir>/camcraft/recipes`.\n\n`ApplyCutRecipe` wraps `CreateOperation`. One undo removes the new operation. MCP tools `save_cut_recipe`, `list_cut_recipes`, and `apply_cut_recipe` use this library. Each tool accepts an optional `library` path. The generated MCP reference and the guide list the tools.\n\nThe caller supplies the new source. The command refuses a recipe by name if its saved parameters contain geometry that the API cannot replace. The audit covers:\n\n- Drill holes and cross holes; bore and thread holes.\n- Contour chain overrides and excluded deburr edges.\n- Tilted plane origins.\n- Circular centers, slot endpoints, probe targets, and undercut endpoints.\n- Wire start and sync points; sinker burn positions.\n\nThe command also refuses a missing tool, an unknown material, and a material mismatch. When a recipe names a material, the destination must have that material in force. An absent destination material now causes a refusal with the recipe name.\n\nThe library format stays the same. The decision record is `docs/decisions/3073-cut-recipes.md`.\n\n## Review fixes and pin proof\n\nThe review found two defects. Applying a recipe copied geometry from its previous source. The material check also accepted an absent destination material.\n\nRegression pins in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe/safety.rs`:\n\n- `cut_recipe_does_not_transfer_holes_to_a_different_source`: transfer between plates with holes at different coordinates.\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_other_saved_coordinates_by_name`: other operations with saved coordinates.\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_saved_picks_and_plane_origins`: cross holes, entity picks, and tilted plane origins.\n- `cut_recipe_with_a_named_material_requires_a_destination_material`: command refusal when the destination material is absent.\n- `cut_recipe_mcp_refuses_an_absent_destination_material`: MCP refusal for the same case.\n\nThe four original tests in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe.rs` also cover save, load, apply, generation, undo, and the existing refusals.\n\nMutation evidence: Removing the geometry guard made all three geometry pins fail. Restoring the old material guard made both absent-material pins fail. After restoration, all nine recipe tests passed. The final quick gate ran the restored pins again.\n\n## Final validation\n\nHead: `e8eb8429461c63a4df20d11dca24e0a71582c34f`\nBase: `upstream/main`, fetched for this gate at `6e641dac753020bfed49fec310237eed28448141`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 337 steps, 2,666 tests passed, zero failures, 22 ignored (36.6 minutes).\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 206 steps, zero gate failures, 46 tests passed (28.2 minutes). Two registered known-fail tests failed as expected; the gate accepted these results: `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` (#1950) and `shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` (#2849).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n- `app suites: example_catalog`: GREEN. 37 tests passed, four ignored (18.58 seconds). This suite ran in the quick gate. Heavy step 53 ran the four ignored cases; all passed. Combined catalog result: 41 of 41 passed.\n- `mcp_doc_drift`: GREEN.\n- Other reached golden suites: GREEN. All 27 reached suites with direct golden checks passed: `adaptive_trochoid`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_css`, `lathe_post_g76`, `lathe_post_inch`, `lathe_post_thread_dips`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread`, `pocket_no_adaptive`, `pocket3d_trochoid`, `probe_op`, `program_entry`, `rest_pocket`, `sinker_burn`, `sinker_orbit`, `sinker_side`, `sinker_undersize`, `sinker_wear`, `slot_dxf_sketch`, `thread_boss`, `thread_mill`, `v_carve_op`, `wear_comp`, `contour_start_point`, `control_comp`, `corner_relief`, and `first_router_part`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. After the catalog suite ran, no recorded program or golden file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The first quick run hit seeded-artifact error `E0463`. An isolated target clean and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` resolved it. The final quick run passed.\n- UI screenshots do not apply. This PR changes no UI files.\n- There is no GUI recipe panel. Issue #3393 holds that work.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill has no row for the new tools. This PR supplies the generated reference and guide entries.\n- Recipes omit coolant and area controls. Coolant depends on the machine. Area controls depend on the geometry.\n- Automatic geometry matching is not exercised. The command refuses recipes that need replacement geometry.\n- The knowledge graph could not be updated because `graphify` is not installed on this host.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Saved cut recipes: save an operation's settings under a name and apply them to new geometry in one undoable step (MCP `save_cut_recipe`, `list_cut_recipes`, `apply_cut_recipe`); a recipe whose tool or material is gone is refused by name.\n\nFixes #3073\n",
